{"The Check method falls through to query the database when cached permissions exist but the specific resource check fails (allowed=false), defeating the purpose of the cache for negative checks and creating unnecessary DB load": 0.6590951681137085, "Cache key construction uses simple string concatenation with underscore delimiters, creating ambiguity and potential collision risks when fields contain underscores or are empty": 0.25963547825813293, "Denial cache check happens before evaluating cached permissions, meaning users who gain permission after being denied will continue to be denied until the denial cache entry expires": 0.7150111794471741, "TTL-only invalidation creates lingering denials - the denial cache lacks mutation-triggered invalidation, so users may remain denied after permission grants or resource moves until TTL expiry": 0.6473511457443237}